        description = 'WEEKEND CAMP- Registration open March 2nd-March 16th  

Robbers Cave State Park, OK 

Interested in taking a break from classes? Come join us in a relaxing weekend of camping and hiking through Robbers Cave State Park. In this trip you will get to explore some of the same caves where famous robbers such as Jesse James used to hide out! 

Starting early in the morning, we will drive together as a group to Robbers Cave State Park. Once we arrive, we’ll set up our campsite and begin exploring the park’s scenic trails. Throughout the weekend, we’ll hike through forests, scramble across rocky outcrops, and visit the historic caves. In the evenings, we’ll unwind around the campfire, enjoy dinner, and settle in under the stars. After packing up on Sunday morning, we’ll make the drive back to UNT, arriving by mid to late afternoon. 

Upon registering for this trip, you will be required to attend a mandatory pre-trip meeting on March 17th from 7:00pm – 8:00pm. Here you will meet your trip leaders and fellow participants, receive more in-depth information about the trip and what to bring, and provide our staff with medical and emergency contact information. 

  

Any questions regarding this trip can be directed towards staff at the following facilities: 

UNT Outdoor Pursuits Center 

1:00pm - 6:00pm Thur-Mon (closed Wednesday)  

(940) 369-8349 

  

UNT Climbing Wall 

3:00pm – 8:00pm Sun-Fri, 3:00pm – 7:00pm Sat 

(940) 369-8609',
