updated_existing_event AS (
    UPDATE events
    SET
        title = 'Weekend Paddle at Brazos River, TX',
        description = 'WEEKEND PADDLE: Registration open April 6-20

Brazos River, TX 

Float along the same historic river the conquistadors explored, and the Comanche Native Americans used to hide from US Cavalry. This two-day trip will show you 20 miles of the "Mississippi of Texas."

Starting early in the morning, we will drive together as a group to the Brazos River, located a few hours from Denton. Once we arrive, we’ll load our boats and begin our two-day paddling adventure down one of Texas’s most historic waterways. In the evening, we’ll set up camp along the river, cook dinner, and relax under the stars. After finishing the final miles of our paddle on Sunday, we’ll pack up and head back to UNT by mid to late afternoon. 

Upon registering for this trip, you will be required to attend a mandatory pre-trip meeting on April 21st from 7:00pm – 8:00pm. Here you will meet your trip leaders and fellow participants, receive more in-depth information about the trip and what to bring, and provide our staff with medical and emergency contact information. 

  

Any questions regarding this trip can be directed towards staff at the following facilities: 

UNT Outdoor Pursuits Center 

1:00pm - 6:00pm Thur-Mon (closed Wednesday)  

(940) 369-8349 

  

UNT Climbing Wall 

3:00pm – 8:00pm Sun-Fri, 3:00pm – 7:00pm Sat 

(940) 369-8609',
        location_id = (SELECT location_id FROM resolved_location),
        start_date_time = TIMESTAMP '2026-04-26 00:00:00',
        end_date_time = TIMESTAMP '2026-04-27 00:00:00',
